            <ArticleTitle>[Microsymptoms in leptospirosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2637-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leptospirosis is not an exotic disease, still it is seen more frequent in southern countries. Microsymptoms, such as supraorbital headache, muscle pain in the legs, herpes naso-labialis or axillaris (often symmetrical), pharynxenanthema, fugitive rash, epistaxis, confusion, etc., are very important for early diagnosis. An intradermal test for early diagnosis was developed and is described here.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
